actor "Finder" as Actor
participant "Proposed Finder Reservation" as Page
participant "Proposed Claims API" as API
participant "Proposed Reservation Service" as Service
participant "claims" as Table <<entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Open Release reservation and reopen another claim
activate Page
Page -> API: 2: Release peer reservation (proposed interface)
activate API
API -> API: 3: Validate access session, role and input
alt Valid request
API -> Service: 4: Release reservation and reopen another claim
activate Service
Service -> Service: 5: Require actual Finder; explicit cancellation/no-show review reason
Service -> Table: 6: Proposed: lock and inspect Finder reservation
activate Table
Table --> Service: 7: Active peer reservation
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 8: Check no completed handover, dispute or custody transfer
Service -> Table: 9: Proposed: release reservation while retaining history
activate Table
Table --> Service: 10: Released reservation
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 11: Reopen eligibility for another separate claim, not auto-approve
Service --> API: 12: Reservation released
API --> Page: 13: HTTP 200: Reservation released
Page --> Actor: 14: Show authorized result
deactivate Service
else Invalid input, missing session or insufficient role
API --> Page: 4.1: Proposed rejection: invalid input / authorization
Page --> Actor: 4.2: Show appropriate error; retain form/draft
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

